title: Relations with the Empire
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/reichstag_2.jpg
view-if: marcher_in_government == 1 and foreign_minister_party == "Marcher" and imperial_relations_timer <= 0
on-arrival: imperial_relations_timer += 8; month_actions += 1
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet

= Relations with the Empire

The Empire-in-Exile waits across the northern frontier, and two factions contend at its court. The Empress Jacqueline would see the Commonwealth return as a crowned constituent realm, by treaty rather than by force. The Hardliners want its total subjugation. Which faction prevails depends in large part on us. A Commonwealth that is strong, stable, and defended makes the Empress's case for her, and a weak and divided one is the Hardliners' best argument. The Foreign Ministry must decide how to conduct itself toward the Empire.

The attachés' reading of us: our forces are [+ military_readiness : military_readiness +], and the northern court judges the Commonwealth [+ commonwealth_standing : commonwealth_standing +].

- @disarmament: Propose mutual disarmament.
- @reconciliation: Open quiet talks of reconciliation.
- @moderates: Contact the moderate elements of the Empire-in-Exile.
- @saber_rattle: Rattle the saber, and let the Empire see our resolve.
- @extradite: Extradite the anti-Imperial exiles as a gesture of good faith.
- @return: Hold our present course.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@disarmament
subtitle: Scale back the shipyards and the garrisons in exchange for the same from the Empire. (Requires the War Ministry.)
choose-if: army_minister_party == "Marcher" and army_strength > 0
unavailable-subtitle: We must hold the War Ministry to negotiate disarmament.
on-arrival: empire_posture += 8 if empire_posture < 100; army_strength -= 15 if army_strength > 0; army_militancy -= 0.3 if army_militancy > 0; nationalism -= 5 if nationalism > 0; pacifism += 1; west_relation += 1;

We scale back the shipyards and thin the frontier garrisons, and the Empire, watched by Ethia, does the same. Tensions ease, and the Empress's position at her court is strengthened. A Commonwealth that disarms should be sure that the Empress, and not her Hardliners, will still hold the reins when the treaties come due.

@reconciliation
subtitle: Open quiet talks. Ease the War Loans and the frontier disputes in exchange for lower tensions.
on-arrival: empire_posture += 7 if empire_posture < 100; budget += 1; nationalism -= 2 if nationalism > 0; dufour_angry -= 5; left_dissent += 2; pro_republic -= 1 if pro_republic > 0;

Through back channels we let it be known that the Commonwealth would welcome an easing of tensions, and the Empress's envoys respond in kind with a softening of the War Loans and a quiet word on the frontier. [? if president == "DuFour": President DuFour, who wants above all to spare the realms another war, is gratified. ?][? if president != "DuFour": The presidential palace signals its approval. ?] Our own benches mutter about appeasement, and Left dissent rises slightly.

@moderates
subtitle: Quiet courtesies to the Empress's conciliators. Small gestures that strengthen the peace party at the northern court.
on-arrival: empire_posture += 5 if empire_posture < 100; dufour_angry -= 3; nationalism -= 1 if nationalism > 0; left_dissent += 1

Nothing is signed and nothing is promised. But letters from the moderate lords of the Empire-in-Exile are answered promptly and warmly, their names are remembered at receptions, and their journals receive interviews that the Hardliners' journals do not. At the northern court, where standing counts for a great deal, the Empress's peace party is strengthened by it. Our own Left notes sourly whom we have been writing to.

@saber_rattle
subtitle: A show of resolve. Popular at home, but the Empire's reading of it depends on whether we are strong enough to back it.
on-arrival: nationalism += 5; pro_republic += 2; army_militancy += 0.3; imperial_fear -= 1 if imperial_fear > 0; empire_posture += 4 if commonwealth_standing >= 55; empire_posture -= 6 if commonwealth_standing < 55;

We answer the Empire's posturing with our own: a review of the fleet, a hard speech, and a closing of ranks. At home it is met with a surge of defiant pride, and nationalist feeling rises. [? if commonwealth_standing >= 55: The Empress's moderates draw the lesson that the Commonwealth is too strong and too sure to be had cheaply, and that a treaty is the better bargain. The Empire's posture warms. ?][? if commonwealth_standing < 55: But the Hardliners, who see our weakness, take it as the provocation they have been waiting for. Bluster from a republic that cannot back it only proves their case, and the Empire's posture hardens. ?]

@extradite
subtitle: Hand over the anti-Imperial exiles sheltering in the Commonwealth. (Requires the Justice Ministry.)
choose-if: justice_minister_party == "Marcher"
unavailable-subtitle: We must hold the Justice Ministry to order the extraditions.
on-arrival: empire_posture += 6 if empire_posture < 100; pro_republic -= 3 if pro_republic > 0; collectivist_relation -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1 if (in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition); left_dissent += 3;

We hand the exiles over to the Empress: the pamphleteers, the deserters, and the old enemies of the throne who fled south for our protection. The gesture is not lost on her court, and the Hardliners lose an argument. But it is a shameful business, illiberal and cold, and support for the republic falls. The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, who counted many of the exiles as their own, will not soon forgive it, and relations with them fall.
